## Context
Author decision relayed by the git-erg session (2026-11-09): the harness drives the rollout of
required ID claims (git-erg 0306/0307) to every erg store on padme and doudou. Pin, not release:
every repo takes the binary with sha256
`dafb1d48f2ce5b380e790244d958678b9eea307d9d16588c1358dddf4dc15a58` (git-erg rev 8d24e74,
commit aee15dd); if git-erg main has moved, stop and ask git-erg. A signed release comes later.
git-erg's dry run on scratch copies: all 25 stores migrate, zero blockers.

## Recipe (one PR per repo, one host, fresh worktree)
1. fetch; skip if origin/main already has `tickets/.claims/`
2. `tickets/erg sync --upstream`; 3. check `tickets/erg version` shows the sha256
4. `tickets/erg migrate --claims tickets`; 5. `tickets/erg init`
6. tracked core.hooksPath: `tickets/erg install --hooks`, review the chaining, commit it
7. the repo's own gate; 8. merge by the repo's process.
After landing: every other clone pulls; per-clone hooks run `tickets/erg install --hooks`.
Branch cut before migration: rebase, `tickets/erg migrate --claims tickets`, commit. Duplicate
number: migrate lists it and writes nothing; renumber one by hand, rerun.
Each repo's migration runs under that repo's own rules (rules/workflow.md, Cross-project work):
its own session, or one launched there; the harness tracks, it does not edit other repos.

